From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 13:28:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add SwiftUI battle and upgrades UI with `GameState` model

### Motivation

- Provide a simple fantasy-styled UI that displays hero/enemy HP, names, and a battle log while offering a separate upgrades screen to modify stats.
- Bind the visible UI state to a single source of truth so interactions update the model reactively via `GameState`.

### Description

- Add a new `GameState` ObservableObject with published properties for names, HP, stats, `battleLog`, and methods `increaseAttack()` and `increaseDefense()`.
- Add app entry `FirstProjectApp.swift` that injects `GameState` into the environment for child views.
- Introduce `ContentView.swift` (RootView) containing `TabView` with `BattleView` and `UpgradesView`, plus `CharacterCard` and `UpgradeStatView` components that bind to `GameState` for HP, names, log, and upgrade actions.
- Add `Colors.swift` with a lightweight fantasy color palette and update views to use the new color extensions (e.g. `.accentGold`, `.nightSky`, `.heroGreen`).

### Testing

- No automated tests were executed for these UI-only changes.
